+# AUDIT REPORT 20261007-191022 (PRE-audit, plan review)
+PATCH: N/A (PRE-audit of implementation plan for issue #275; no code diff exists yet)
+FILES: userspace/ramdiskd.c, src/kernel/task/taskdefs.cpp, src/kernel/daemon/daemon_mgr.cpp, src/kernel/kernel.cpp (DaemonWatch), src/kernel/test/test_ramdisk.cpp (all planned only)
+
+## FINDINGS
+- [S2] plan (DaemonWatch row for ramdiskd) — contradicts documented closed boot gate and couples boot timing to ramdiskd
+  WHY: taskdefs.cpp:92 documents "kernel.cpp DaemonWatch stays vfsd/iocd/watchdogd only", and a FAILED/missing ramdiskd would force every boot down the 500-tick degraded path (kernel.cpp:402-430), implicating the #45 per-stage boot-timing budgets — the plan must state gate membership explicitly and reconcile the comment either way.
+- [S2] plan (10-chunk read_block/write_block loop) — send_sync reply-matching discipline not mandated
+  WHY: send_sync pops the oldest queued message with no sender matching, so any grant or stale reply in the client inbox during the 10-message chunk loop is eaten as a "reply" and fails the call (LEARNINGS #16/#296) — the plan must mandate drain-before-send_sync (plain recv, no authorize) or sender-matched reply waits on both client and daemon sides.
+- [S2] plan (wire: block/chunk geometry) — bounds validation not explicitly mandated for reachable IPC input
+  WHY: Block number and chunk index arrive over IPC, so §5 requires explicit fail-closed error returns (block < 32768, chunk_idx < 10, tail-len clamp offset+len <= 512) with §10.5 named bounds — geometry alone (8 B header + ≤56 B data, 10 chunks/block) does not state the checks.
+- [S3] plan (boot-time 16 MiB UntypedMem::create) — carve point ordering not pinned
+  WHY: 4096 contiguous user pages starve if carved after fragmenting boot allocs, so the plan should name an early carve point (before driver/DMA pool setup) with the already-stated fail-closed degraded path; is_user=true is correct and load-bearing (frame_map.cpp:79 refuses non-user maps).
+- [S3] plan (re-grant hook) — restart-path placement and stale-handle semantics unstated
+  WHY: Restart (restart_stale_daemons and ensure_running, daemon_mgr.cpp:195-324) mints a new task/CSpace, so the plan must place the re-grant on both paths and state that stale client handles fail closed on lookup (cap.cpp stale-gen rule); blast radius is test-only in this increment (no production client yet).
+- [S3] plan (SS budget 2+3+1+2=8/10) — schedulability justification not recorded
+  WHY: 0.8 exceeds the Liu-Layland n=4 sufficient bound (0.757), which is fine only because all four periods are identical (harmonic sets are RM-schedulable to 1.0) — the plan should record that one-line justification; daemon_mgr ternary yielding 2 needs no change (verified daemon_mgr.cpp:223-224,316-317).
+- [S3] plan (tests: 4 stub-first in test_ramdisk.cpp, storage aggregate) — count-row and wiring updates unstated
+  WHY: Adding 4 tests moves the storage expected-count row (148 in test_expected_counts.hpp:284) and needs the THREE wirings plus aggregate membership per LEARNINGS #198; also note initrd size growth from the new daemon ELF.
+- [S3] plan (torn writes documented acceptable) — follow-up must revisit before executable use
+  WHY: Documented torn-write tolerance is acceptable for scratch-block use in this increment, but the loadelf-from-ramdisk follow-up must add checksums or quiescence before executing torn-loaded images.
+
+## PATCH
+No `audits/rejected_patch.diff` at PRE stage (no code exists to correct; per instruction no code was written) — cure is plan amendment: (1) resolve DaemonWatch gate membership + reconcile the taskdefs.cpp:92 comment, (2) mandate the #296 drain/sender-match discipline in the chunk loop, (3) mandate explicit block/chunk bounds checks with named constants and fail-closed codes, (4) pin the early carve point, re-grant placement, harmonic-budget note, count-row bump, and the loadelf atomicity revisit.
+
+DECISION: REJECTED
